[UsaMap]
<p>
The map is #N($1800, $04, $04) by #N($0C00, $04, $04) units, listed
at #R$7811 as #N$197 points. Each point is an obstacle, a cup or a
place. Places have bit 6 set and take their names from #R$722F;
they are the fuel stops from Los Angeles in the west to New York
in the east. Cups have sprite ID #N$20. Their X is fixed, and
#R$6498 picks a new Y from #N$20 to #N$9F each round; the gold
cups sit in the middle of that band, and the dotted line is the
range. The red car is the start written to #R$5E05 and #R$5E08. Y
counts up from the south, as on the sidebar drawn by #R$6949. The
picture uses the daytime colours from #R$6BE6 on the yellow play
area. Drag to move, and use the mouse wheel or pinch to zoom.
</p>
#HTML(<div class="usa-map-viewer" id="usa-map-viewer"></div>)
<p class="usa-map-hint">Drag to move. Scroll or pinch to zoom.</p>

[Credits]
<div class="box box-1">
  This disassembly would have taken a lot longer to finish if it weren't for the
  research and documentation already done and made available by:
#LIST
  { <a href="https://mrcook.uk/">Michael R. Cook</a> }
LIST#
  This game shares a lot of functionality with Jetpac, hence his disassembly was
  invaluable!
</div>

[Expand]
#DEF(#NOCROP(addr,size,attr)(fname) #UDGARRAY($size,attr=$attr,scale=4,step=$size,mask=1,flip=2)(($addr)-($addr + ({height} * $size) - $size)-$01-($size * $08))($fname))
#DEF(#CROP(addr,size,attr)(fname) #UDGARRAY($size,attr=$attr,scale=4,step=$size,mask=1,flip=2)(($addr)-($addr + ({height} * $size) - $size)-$01-($size * $08)){$00, $04 * ($08 - ({height} % $08)), $04 * $size * $08, $04 * {height}}($fname))

#DEF(#SPRITE(id,base=$7F06,attr=$07)(fname)
  #LET(offset=$id * $02)
  #LET(addr=#PEEK($base + {offset}) + #PEEK($base + {offset} + $01) * $100)
  #LET(height=#PEEK({addr}))#IF({height} % $08)(#CROP({addr} + $01, $02, $attr)($fname),#NOCROP({addr} + $01, $02, $attr)($fname)))

#DEF(#SPRITENAME(id)
  #MAP($id)(
    ?,
    0:"Cactus",
    1:"USA Sign",
    2:"Bush",
    3:"Flower",
    4:"Boulder",
    5:"Tree",
    6:"Fuel Pump",
